      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ITERATIVE IMPORTANCE SAMPLING WITH MARKOV CHAIN MONTE CARLO SAMPLING",
      "bbox": [
        146.2434539794922,
        76.2531967163086,
        502.4859619140625,
        82.44593811035156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Substituting eq. (23) into eq. (6), we ﬁnally obtain the following estimate for the combined ESS",
      "bbox": [
        122.11600494384766,
        98.08998107910156,
        538.6422119140625,
        106.93677520751953
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ESS ≈ESSMCMC",
      "bbox": [
        267.7749938964844,
        112.80500793457031,
        343.6733703613281,
        128.39178466796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N",
      "bbox": [
        317.5870056152344,
        126.37898254394531,
        325.596923828125,
        135.22576904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "· ESSIS.",
      "bbox": [
        347.57000732421875,
        118.98709869384766,
        380.9476013183594,
        129.3059844970703
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(24)",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        119.54499816894531,
        127.87451171875,
        128.39178466796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "So, what is new in eq. (24) with respect to eq. (7) is the factor ESSMCMC",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        138.63626098632812,
        439.8727111816406,
        149.4927978515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N",
      "bbox": [
        418.8219909667969,
        146.15615844726562,
        425.1332702636719,
        152.34889221191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "which accounts for a",
      "bbox": [
        445.94000244140625,
        140.6459503173828,
        538.5624389648438,
        149.49273681640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reduction in eﬀective sample size due to the correlation of the MCMC samples (a reduction since",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        152.60096740722656,
        538.5628051757812,
        161.44775390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "it is very unlikely that the correlation will be negative).",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        164.5569610595703,
        353.03924560546875,
        173.40374755859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4. Importance sampling over a set of probability distributions",
      "bbox": [
        162.62301635742188,
        185.5559844970703,
        486.0867004394531,
        194.40277099609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Let M ⊂Rd be a compact set and pt(·) = {p(·|t)|t ∈M} be a probability density function",
      "bbox": [
        122.11601257324219,
        199.8739776611328,
        538.600341796875,
        213.2499542236328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "parameterized by t (i.e. hyperparameters). The lower expectation of a function f with respect to",
      "bbox": [
        110.16094970703125,
        215.44398498535156,
        538.5577392578125,
        224.290771484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pt for all t ∈M is assumed to exist and is estimated by",
      "bbox": [
        110.16094970703125,
        226.84109497070312,
        353.2247314453125,
        237.74078369140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(25)",
      "bbox": [
        110.16094207763672,
        248.31398010253906,
        127.87444305419922,
        257.1607666015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "E(f) := min",
      "bbox": [
        263.4156188964844,
        247.9679718017578,
        316.45904541015625,
        257.1607666015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "t∈M",
      "bbox": [
        299.27899169921875,
        256.4237060546875,
        317.0246276855469,
        263.0069580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Z",
      "bbox": [
        318.6820068359375,
        241.26953125,
        324.2212219238281,
        247.6455841064453
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "f(x)pt(x)dx.",
      "bbox": [
        330.30499267578125,
        248.31398010253906,
        385.3186950683594,
        258.075927734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In practice, one can search for the minimum using numerical methods. For instance, an iterative",
      "bbox": [
        122.115966796875,
        269.2289733886719,
        538.592529296875,
        278.07574462890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "version of standard importance sampling has been used to estimate bounds on expectations in",
      "bbox": [
        110.16096496582031,
        281.1839599609375,
        538.5926513671875,
        290.0307312011719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "robust Bayesian analysis [14, 41, 42, 43].",
      "bbox": [
        110.16096496582031,
        293.1389465332031,
        286.8476257324219,
        301.9857177734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Using importance sampling, the lower expectation is estimated by",
      "bbox": [
        122.115966796875,
        305.09393310546875,
        410.21441650390625,
        313.9407043457031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(26)",
      "bbox": [
        110.16096496582031,
        329.096923828125,
        127.87446594238281,
        337.9436950683594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "bE(f) ≈min",
      "bbox": [
        254.79396057128906,
        328.5390319824219,
        305.732666015625,
        339.47052001953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "t∈M",
      "bbox": [
        288.5559997558594,
        337.2066345214844,
        306.3016357421875,
        343.7898864746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PN",
      "bbox": [
        309.1540222167969,
        319.2881774902344,
        325.9812927246094,
        327.6425476074219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i=1 f(Xi)wt(Xi)",
      "bbox": [
        319.6700134277344,
        322.2229309082031,
        389.96441650390625,
        334.0587158203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PN",
      "bbox": [
        321.78900146484375,
        334.8411865234375,
        338.61627197265625,
        343.195556640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i=1 wt(Xi)",
      "bbox": [
        332.30499267578125,
        337.77593994140625,
        377.3304138183594,
        349.6117248535156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ",",
      "bbox": [
        391.1589660644531,
        329.0969543457031,
        393.9285583496094,
        337.9437255859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where wt(x) := cpt(x)",
      "bbox": [
        110.16098022460938,
        353.4861755371094,
        201.34930419921875,
        366.0058898925781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "q(x) .",
      "bbox": [
        183.17100524902344,
        356.24395751953125,
        205.31761169433594,
        368.5267333984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Iterative importance sampling estimates the lower expectation of a function f by moving the",
      "bbox": [
        122.11600494384766,
        369.33795166015625,
        538.5689697265625,
        378.1847229003906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sampling distribution, q, towards the optimal distribution [14, 41]. The stopping criterion is that",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        381.2929382324219,
        538.6239013671875,
        390.13970947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the eﬀective sample size of importance sampling should be close enough to the desired indepen-",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        393.2479248046875,
        538.562744140625,
        402.0946960449219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dent sample size (denoted by ESStarget) that is ﬁxed in advance. In this paper, we adapt iterative",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        405.20391845703125,
        538.597900390625,
        414.96484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "importance sampling introduced in [14, 41, 42]. Our contribution is the eﬀective sample size of im-",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        417.1589050292969,
        538.5926513671875,
        426.00567626953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "portance sampling with correlated MCMC samples which allows us to combine iterative importance",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        429.1138916015625,
        538.5726928710938,
        437.9606628417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sampling with MCMC sampling, thus allowing for robust analysis of more complex models. It is",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        441.0688781738281,
        538.6026000976562,
        449.9156494140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "important to highlight that how large the sample size for MCMC samples should be and ESStarget",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        453.02386474609375,
        538.0596313476562,
        462.7857971191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in step 2 and step 4 respectively, are values ﬁxed in advance (i.e. they are inputs to the procedure).",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        464.9788513183594,
        538.6027221679688,
        473.82562255859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The method goes as follows:",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        476.9348449707031,
        233.1891326904297,
        485.7816162109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 1: Set t = t0 where t0 is an initial value in the feasible region.",
      "bbox": [
        132.85400390625,
        487.48486328125,
        430.38018798828125,
        499.9466247558594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 2: Generate samples from q(x) = pt(x) using MCMC sampling until the eﬀective sample",
      "bbox": [
        132.85403442382812,
        503.0548400878906,
        538.5723266601562,
        512.8167724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "size for the MCMC sample is large enough (i.e. exceed a speciﬁed threshold).",
      "bbox": [
        144.80899047851562,
        515.0108032226562,
        482.5212707519531,
        523.8576049804688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 3: Find t∗= arg mint∈M",
      "bbox": [
        132.85398864746094,
        530.23779296875,
        268.1376037597656,
        539.998779296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PN",
      "bbox": [
        271.48797607421875,
        525.3578491210938,
        285.2198791503906,
        530.7761840820312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i=1 f(Xi)wt(Xi)",
      "bbox": [
        279.8599853515625,
        526.9820556640625,
        338.4513244628906,
        535.416748046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PN",
      "bbox": [
        281.7799987792969,
        535.2059326171875,
        295.5108947753906,
        540.38427734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i=1 wt(Xi)",
      "bbox": [
        290.1510009765625,
        536.5901489257812,
        328.1603088378906,
        545.02490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "using an optimization algorithm.",
      "bbox": [
        342.9709777832031,
        530.2379150390625,
        485.8844299316406,
        539.084716796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 4: If ESS > ESStarget, or maximum number of iterations reached, then stop.",
      "bbox": [
        132.85397338867188,
        544.6729125976562,
        492.9004211425781,
        554.4338989257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 5: Set t = t∗and go to Step 2.",
      "bbox": [
        132.85397338867188,
        556.6279296875,
        293.8263244628906,
        566.388916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The convergence of the method depends on the distributions and the parameter space. We have",
      "bbox": [
        122.1159896850586,
        570.7939453125,
        538.5927124023438,
        579.6407470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "set a maximum number of iterations (i.e. in our case, 10 000) to stop the algorithm when it does",
      "bbox": [
        110.1609878540039,
        582.7489013671875,
        538.5825805664062,
        591.595703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "not converge.",
      "bbox": [
        110.1609878540039,
        594.7039184570312,
        168.03372192382812,
        603.5507202148438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The condition of a large enough sample size is added in Step 2 to ensure that the optimization",
      "bbox": [
        122.1159896850586,
        606.658935546875,
        538.6027221679688,
        615.5057373046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in Step 3 is based on a reliable sample. For example, in the application below, we ﬁrst specify the",
      "bbox": [
        110.1609878540039,
        618.6139526367188,
        538.6026000976562,
        627.4607543945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ESStarget and then we require the eﬀective sample size for the MCMC samples to be 20% greater",
      "bbox": [
        110.1609878540039,
        630.5689697265625,
        538.5465087890625,
        640.9107666015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "than the ESStarget. The stopping criterion in Step 4 uses the eﬀective sample size for importance",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        642.52490234375,
        538.5587768554688,
        652.285888671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
  ],
